! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 7's COMPARISON DRIVER -- the
! block docs/NEXT.md item 1 has wanted since the scouting pass.  PDF
! p.71 (printed p.68), octal 022346.40-022401.00, transcribed VERBATIM
! at the listing's own addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_160105_listing.py.
!
! THIS IS THE POSITIVE BOUNDARY-INTERRUPT CASE.  pp.65 and 68 test
! whether the boundary REGISTERS HOLD THEIR BITS
! (ax5b_16099_ub_data.strap, ax5b_160102_lb_ctl.strap).  This one
! tests whether the COMPARISON FIRES -- it sets boundaries, ENABLES,
! fetches from an address outside them, and expects an address-
! -monitoring interruption.  The deck's own summary, from the comment
! column:
!
!     -TEST THE COMPARE CKTS, SETUP INTERRUPT TABLE.  UB HAS X, LB HAS
!     -X-2.  FETCH FROM X+1 TO CHK UB COMP, FROM X-3 TO CHK LB COMP,
!     -AND FROM X-1 TO CHECK WITHIN RANGE OF X IS FROM 000040 THRU
!     -777777 OCTAL.
!
! So: upper bound X, lower bound X-2, and three fetches -- one above,
! one below, one inside -- swept across the whole address range.
!
! IT IS INTERRUPT-DRIVEN, which is what makes it the hard one.  It
! builds the interruption table by copying I60K12 through it
! ("SX,$X2,I60IT($X1)" in a CB+ loop), points entry 16 at I60107,
! calls SSIP's save/restore through "SIC,I60SX1 / B,I60S1", clears the
! first-interrupt flags I60AD1/I60AD3, sets the bounds, enables with
! "BE,$+.32", does the fetch, and lands in one of two places the deck
! labels for itself: I60107 "-AD INTRPTS ENTER HERE." and I6010A
! "-ALL INTRPTS EXCEPT AD ENTER HERE."
!
! AND IT USES TRANSMIT IMMEDIATE.  "TI,1,BOUND1,3.0" moves one word
! into word 3 -- the boundary register itself -- and it is a FULL WORD
! at an ODD half-word (022365.40, straddling into 022366.00), the same
! shape as p.45's two TIs.  Until TRANSMIT_CODES landed earlier today
! this block could not have been assembled at all; this is the first
! use of TI outside the page it was derived for.
!
! ENCODING ONLY, and the reason is specific: it cannot run without
! I60S1's body (the SSIP save/restore subroutine at 022741.00, still
! not transcribed -- see docs/NEXT.md), the interruption table I60IT
! at 023201.00, and the boundary control words BOUND0/BOUND1 at
! 023302/023303.  Those are the harness item 1 has always needed, and
! this block is where the need is real rather than assumed.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: none, and the "none" replaces one.  This header used
! to read "numeric labels are prefixed L (160105, 160106, 160107,
! 160108, 160109, 16010A, 160110, 160111, 160122, 160IT, 160XW1,
! 160XW3, 160K12, 160SX1, 160S1, 160AD1, 160AD3)", the prefix being
! needed because this assembler reads a leading digit as an address.
! The glyph was measured at 600 dpi and it is the LETTER I, so those
! names are I60105, I60106, ... I60AD3 as the page prints them, legal
! STRAP-1 symbols unaided and written here unaltered
! (docs/listing_typography.md).  Nothing else is changed; every
! external is given by SYN at the address this block's own rows print
! for it.

I60XW1 SYN, (8)23065.0
I60K12 SYN, (8)23055.0
I60IT  SYN, (8)23201.0
INT     SYN, (8)1353.0
I60XW3 SYN, (8)23067.0
BOUND0  SYN, (8)23302.0
BOUND1  SYN, (8)23303.0
BIT57   SYN, (8)24613.0
I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0
I60AD1 SYN, (8)23063.0
I60AD3 SYN, (8)23064.0
I60122 SYN, (8)22506.40
I60110 SYN, (8)22401.40
I60111 SYN, (8)22414.0
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0
        SLC, (8)22346.40
I60105 LX,  $X1, I60XW1        ! -TEST THE COMPARE CKTS, SETUP
        LX,  $X2, I60K12        ! -INTERRUPT TABLE.  UB HAS X, LB HAS
        SX,  $X2, I60IT($X1)    ! -X-2.  FETCH FROM X+1 TO CHK UB COMP,
        CB+, $X1, $-.32          ! -FROM X-3 TO CHK LB COMP, AND FROM
        LVI, $X1, INT            ! -X-1 TO CHECK WITHIN RANGE OF X IS
        LX,  $X2, I60XW3        ! -FROM 000040 THRU 777777 OCTAL.
        Z,   BOUND0
        LX,  $X13, BIT57
        SX,  $X13, BOUND1
        LVI, $X3, I60107
        SVA, $X3, I60IT+16
        SIC, I60SX1             ! -CLEAR INDS 0-19
        B,   I60S1
        Z,   I60AD1             ! -CLEAR FIRST INTERRUPT INDICATORS
        Z,   I60AD3
I60106 LVI, $X3, I60107+.32
        SVA, $X3, I60107
        BZB, 4.60, I60122
        LVI, $X3, I60109
        SVA, $X3, I6010A
        BD,  $+.32
        Z,   $MASK               ! -SETUP UB + LB.
        SV,  $X2, BOUND0+.32     ! -LOWER BOUND
        SV,  $X2, BOUND1+.32
        V+I, $X2, 2.0
        SV,  $X2, BOUND0         ! -UPPER BOUND
        SV,  $X2, BOUND1
        Z,   $IND
        BDFZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, BOUND1, 3.0
        SR,  $X1, $IA
        BE,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, 0($X2)        ! -FETCH FROM UB, BC IS 1.
        BD,  $+.32
        SV,  $X1, $IA
        BD,  I60109
I6010A BD,  $+.32               ! -ALL INTRPTS EXCEPT AD ENTER HERE.
I60107 BD,  $+.32               ! -AD INTRPTS ENTER HERE.
        SV,  $X1, $IA
        LV,  $X13, I60AD1       ! -DID WE INTRPT LAST TIME THRU.
        BXVZ, I60108
        LX,  $X15, 3.0
        B,   I60122
I60108 V+I, $X13, (8)777777.40
        SV,  $X13, I60AD1
        B,   I60111             ! -UB FROM AD.
I60109 BDFZ, I60110
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60106
        SIC, SEN0+.32
        B,   SSW                 ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  I60122             ! -TERMINATE.
        END, I60105
